  ('07330743-c16e-473e-a600-6aecc570d1fa','Yolo Bowmen takes its name from Yolo County in California''s Sacramento Valley, and it''s based in Dixon, a farming town between Sacramento and the Bay Area. As a volunteer club, it''s the kind of range kept running by a core group of members rather than paid staff, typical for smaller agricultural-region clubs across the Central Valley. No programs, course type, or amenities are listed for this location, so what a visit actually looks like isn''t spelled out here. Archers passing through the Dixon-Davis corridor looking for a local club to shoot with should reach out directly to ask about membership and access.'),
  ('52066b07-153e-4db3-9b8e-b27ac71dfedf','York Road Archery Range, in North Royalton south of Cleveland, is listed as a public facility rather than a private club or commercial business, setting it apart from most of the member- or business-run ranges in the area. A public designation generally suggests it''s tied to a municipal or park system rather than requiring membership or paid staff to access, though the specifics of that arrangement aren''t detailed here. No course layout, program, or amenity information is listed for this location. Cleveland-area archers interested in a public option should confirm directly what oversight body runs it and what access actually looks like before planning a visit.'),
  ('5bead3d9-1247-45a7-a07c-eb4a824eea00','Yuba Sutter Bowhunters is a volunteer archery club based in Sutter, a small community in the Sacramento Valley north of Sacramento itself, in the county the club''s name references. As a volunteer club, it likely depends on a core group of local bowhunters to keep the range maintained and running rather than functioning as a public business with posted hours. No course details, programs, or amenities are listed for this listing, typical for smaller rural clubs in this farming region. Archers in the Sutter-Yuba City area interested in bowhunting-focused shooting should contact the club directly to ask about membership and how to get on the range.'),
  ('90d91699-b415-4d64-982d-d3f4283ae8d3','This listing for Yuba Sutter Bowhunters carries a Yuba City address, just across the Feather River from Sutter in the same Sacramento Valley community cluster the club''s name draws from. Like other small volunteer clubs in the region, it appears to run on member involvement rather than a fixed retail schedule, and no course, program, or amenity details are listed here to confirm what''s on-site. Yuba City and Sutter sit close enough together that archers in either town would likely consider this club a local option. Confirming which physical location is current and how to reach the group is best done by contacting them directly rather than relying on an address alone.'),
  ('b42550e2-e825-4120-872b-0b087a6dd200','A second listing under a closely related name, Yuba-Sutter Archery Association is also recorded in Marysville, California, but here as a volunteer club rather than the JOAD- and adult-program-affiliated club listed elsewhere under a similar name. That distinction matters for anyone trying to figure out which entry to contact, since a volunteer club typically runs on member time rather than structured, affiliated programming. No course, lane, or amenity details are given for this specific listing. Archers in the Marysville area should confirm directly which of the local Yuba-Sutter archery groups is currently active and how membership or visiting works before assuming either listing is up to date.')
